# PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER

A production-grade FastAPI AI/ML service, scaffolded from the
`fastapi-ai-scaffold` skill. It bakes in the patterns from `fastapi-ai-patterns`:
clean architecture (router / service / repository), a lifespan-loaded model and
shared `httpx` client, a `/health` (liveness) + `/ready` (readiness) split, JWT
auth, SQLModel + Alembic, an LLM gateway with SSE streaming, input/output
guardrails with a Pydantic validation loop, and tests via `dependency_overrides`.

## Quick start

```bash
uv venv && source .venv/bin/activate
uv pip install -e ".[dev]"
cp .env.example .env            # then fill in real secrets
uvicorn app.main:app --reload   # http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
pytest -q
```

## Layout

```
app/
  main.py            FastAPI app + router wiring
  config.py          pydantic-settings Settings (env-driven)
  lifespan.py        startup/shutdown: model + httpx client + db engine
  logging_config.py  structured JSON logging
  api/
    deps.py          shared dependencies (db session, current user, clients)
    v1/              versioned routes: health, auth, inference
  core/security.py   password hashing + JWT (pinned algorithm)
  db/session.py      engine + session factory
  models/            SQLModel tables
  schemas/           request/response Pydantic models
  services/          business logic (no HTTP concerns)
  repositories/      data access behind an interface
  ml/                model handle + guardrails + validation loop
tests/               TestClient + dependency_overrides + SQLite in-memory
migrations/          Alembic environment
```

## Production notes

- Models load once in `lifespan` (never per request). With N workers you hold N
  copies — size workers by memory.
- `/health` is trivially cheap (liveness). `/ready` checks the DB and that the
  model is warm (readiness). Wire them to your orchestrator accordingly.
- Run under Gunicorn with Uvicorn workers in production: see `gunicorn_conf.py`.
- Treat LLM output as untrusted: see `app/ml/guardrails.py` for the
  generate -> validate -> retry loop.
